  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A lot of virtual cinematographers relied on a camera animations mod to record certain shots before the EAC update. \nWhile this is still possible with paid packages like VRCLens, there is no ways to have a camera automatically move along a path without having to move it manually, which makes recording cinematics impractical. Additionally, camera movement is limited to rotation around a single point. No custom paths like you can in 3D software :(\nSure, you can have a camera operator, but even with smooth-cam, the result is never really ideal, plus the hassle of transferring media could just be cut completely by adding this feature.\nThe ideal camera modifications would be an animation-point system similar to the current camera waypoint, but with an option to blend between them and control the speed/zoom/exposure and such so it plays out automatically at the hit of a button on the camera.",
